WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.585 --> 00:00:02.419
Joe?

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:04.379
It's your cue.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.049
It's time
to cut the umbilical cord.

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:11.637
But I've forged my way
in the dark before,

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.055
I can do it now.

00:00:13.138 --> 00:00:14.348
I have to

00:00:15.265 --> 00:00:17.726
to protect my daughter.

00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:19.603
Congratulations, dad.
It's a boy.

00:00:22.731 --> 00:00:23.565
It's a boy?

00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:26.276
I'm fucked!

00:00:28.403 --> 00:00:29.780
And so is he.

00:00:31.156 --> 00:00:32.741
Welcome home, Forty.

00:00:32.824 --> 00:00:34.618
Maybe we can use
his real name.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.748
We're a family.

00:00:40.582 --> 00:00:43.502
Me, a boy, and his mum,

00:00:43.585 --> 00:00:44.586
who is usually great,

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.046
but occasionally
murders people

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:47.172
with her bare hands.

00:00:47.256 --> 00:00:48.590
So, you have a new baby.

00:00:48.674 --> 00:00:49.508
Yeah.

00:00:50.008 --> 00:00:50.843
Yeah, Henry.

00:00:51.677 --> 00:00:53.303
Yeah, sometimes
we call him "Forty".

00:00:53.387 --> 00:00:54.680
His name's Henry.

00:00:54.763 --> 00:00:56.014
A good therapist
would dig into why

00:00:56.098 --> 00:00:57.641
our child is named after
her dead, addict,

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:58.684
co-dependant brother,

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:00.727
I'd imagined
parenthood would feel

00:01:00.811 --> 00:01:03.021
like an essay
by Nicholson Baker,

00:01:03.856 --> 00:01:06.608
tiny moments
made magnificent.

00:01:06.692 --> 00:01:07.651
Yeah.

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.907
Turns out,
parenthood is groundhog day

00:01:13.991 --> 00:01:15.951
as written
by Jean-Paul Sartre.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:19.913
Joe?

00:01:19.997 --> 00:01:21.790
Despite living
in some Greek myth

00:01:21.874 --> 00:01:24.251
about pushing
a boulder of baby poop

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:25.210
up a hill.

00:01:26.044 --> 00:01:27.379
It's incredible.

00:01:27.462 --> 00:01:28.922
The urge to protect.

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:31.300
I feel it in my bones.

00:01:31.383 --> 00:01:33.302
I would do anything for him.

00:01:34.386 --> 00:01:35.554
What I don't feel

00:01:36.597 --> 00:01:37.848
is connection.

00:01:39.391 --> 00:01:43.437
The more I try to bond,
the more he cries.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:46.273
He knows we don't have it.

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:50.068
Why does my own child
not like me?

00:01:50.152 --> 00:01:52.654
Whenever I hang with Henry
I'm reminded of two things.

00:01:52.738 --> 00:01:54.198
One, he hates me.

00:01:54.281 --> 00:01:56.825
Two, I have to protect him
at all costs

00:01:56.909 --> 00:01:58.076
from what happened to me.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.953
You know, babies can tell

00:02:00.037 --> 00:02:01.622
when your heart's
not in it, Joe.

00:02:01.705 --> 00:02:02.998
-I have wanted--
-Just no.

00:02:03.081 --> 00:02:04.666
I'm sorry.
It's all in my head.

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.126
What are you doing?
Are you bringing him?

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.253
You want me
to leave him in the car?

00:02:08.337 --> 00:02:09.963
It's like bad parenting 101.

00:02:10.047 --> 00:02:12.257
Witnessing us
digging up a body isn't?

00:02:12.841 --> 00:02:15.177
Developmentally, he's barely
any depth perception,

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:16.261
which you should know.

00:02:17.221 --> 00:02:18.305
What I'm hearing

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.558
is that even as I'm doing
everything in my power

00:02:21.642 --> 00:02:23.810
to save my child,
my parenting skills

00:02:23.894 --> 00:02:25.229
aren't up to your standards,
is that right?

00:02:25.312 --> 00:02:27.231
Is this really
what's important right now?

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:29.942
So, Joe, how have you found

00:02:30.025 --> 00:02:31.985
the transition
to fatherhood?

00:02:32.069 --> 00:02:34.279
An existential tangle
of dread and failure,

00:02:34.363 --> 00:02:35.405
oh, and also murder.

00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:36.532
It's great.

00:02:37.616 --> 00:02:40.702
And there he goes
every time I touch him.

00:02:40.786 --> 00:02:42.412
Just fucking let me do it.
Joe!

00:02:42.496 --> 00:02:43.330
-Joe? Joe?
-What?

00:02:45.582 --> 00:02:47.960
Come on.
Come on, let's go. Let's go.

00:02:48.043 --> 00:02:49.253
I'm trying.

00:02:51.338 --> 00:02:52.798
I'm in over my head,

00:02:53.841 --> 00:02:55.592
he said using an idiom

00:02:55.676 --> 00:02:56.969
his son
will never understand

00:02:57.052 --> 00:03:00.013
because it's impossible
to communicate with babies.

00:03:01.056 --> 00:03:02.391
Yeah, right. Exactly.

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.608
I'm gonna do everything
I can.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.781
I just don't know
what that means yet.

00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:19.449
I'd...

00:03:30.544 --> 00:03:31.879
So, what? You don't hate me?

00:03:38.427 --> 00:03:40.387
Yeah. Well, same here.

00:03:41.471 --> 00:03:42.306
Same here.

00:03:43.015 --> 00:03:44.683
Okay. Now it's a good talk.

00:03:44.766 --> 00:03:47.227
Okay, go get some rest.
I got him. Really. Really.

00:03:47.311 --> 00:03:48.812
I got him. Hm-mm, I got him.

00:03:48.896 --> 00:03:49.980
Thank you, thank you.

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.481
Thank you,
thank you, thank you.

00:03:51.565 --> 00:03:53.192
-I love you, Forty.
-Oh...

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:56.695
Okay, Henry.
Coming in hot, Henry. Hey.

00:03:57.905 --> 00:03:59.615
Gotta bank to the left.
Here, look.

00:04:00.282 --> 00:04:02.409
-There we go.
-What's Henry like?

00:04:02.492 --> 00:04:03.577
Oh, he's a terrorist.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.455
-Oh...
-No, he's, he's adorable.

00:04:06.538 --> 00:04:07.706
He's sweet.

00:04:07.789 --> 00:04:09.124
A big fan of Hemmingway
and Fitzgerald.

00:04:09.208 --> 00:04:11.293
I'm not surprised, you've
seen him with the bottle.

00:04:12.586 --> 00:04:15.464
I really hope
he's better than me.

00:04:15.547 --> 00:04:17.799
Hey. I'm sorry, baby.
Had more questions.

00:04:17.883 --> 00:04:19.092
Joe, I'm at the hospital.

00:04:19.593 --> 00:04:20.928
Henry has the measles.

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:24.473
I have been kidnapped,
held at knifepoint,

00:04:24.556 --> 00:04:26.183
held at gunpoint,

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:28.727
lost a finger,
been locked in a cage,

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.729
but in my history of scared,

00:04:31.522 --> 00:04:32.356
this...

00:04:33.649 --> 00:04:35.400
is the most scared
I've ever been.

00:04:36.485 --> 00:04:37.694
You have to get better.

00:04:41.573 --> 00:04:43.283
I haven't always
been the best person,

00:04:44.535 --> 00:04:46.036
but being your dad...

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.290
is changing me.

00:04:50.874 --> 00:04:53.919
What does it mean
to be a good father?

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:55.671
To protect? Yes.

00:04:55.754 --> 00:04:59.633
But can you be a good father
if you're a bad man?

00:05:00.217 --> 00:05:01.635
It's not the kind of father
I wanna be

00:05:01.718 --> 00:05:03.262
and not the kind of mother
you wanna be either,

00:05:03.345 --> 00:05:04.304
thank God.

00:05:05.597 --> 00:05:07.391
Our little scout
will be better for it.

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:20.320
I didn't have good parents.

00:05:21.405 --> 00:05:23.323
But I know
what a good parent does...

00:05:24.491 --> 00:05:25.367
Protect.

00:05:26.577 --> 00:05:28.954
Even if that means
protecting from...

00:05:30.372 --> 00:05:31.206
I'm sorry.

00:05:32.499 --> 00:05:33.667
I'm so sorry.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:35.961
This isn't forever.

00:05:39.131 --> 00:05:40.257
I love you.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.508
More than anything.

00:05:43.468 --> 00:05:44.303
Hey!

00:05:47.014 --> 00:05:48.348
I don't know what to say.

